<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mara Salvatrucha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as MS-13</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mara Salvatrucha, or MS-13, is a criminal gang formed in the 1980s by young Salvadoran immigrants in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/los-angeles">Los Angeles</a>, many of them refugees from the civil war. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">mass deportations</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in the 1990s it spread to El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>, Honduras and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, where it and rival gangs drove homicide rates among the highest in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mara-salvatrucha.jpg" alt="Mara Salvatrucha" width="320" height="144" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SSCreader · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MS-13_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
